  "Question": "\\(\\displaystyle\\frac{(3!)!}{3!}=\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\)",
    "B": "\\(2\\)",
    "C": "\\(6\\)",
    "D": "\\(40\\)",
    "E": "\\(120\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "For a positive integer \\(n\\), the factorial \\(n!\\) is the product of the integers from \\(1\\) through \\(n\\). First evaluate the factorial inside the parentheses: \\(3!=3\\cdot2\\cdot1=6\\). Therefore,\n\\[\n\\frac{(3!)!}{3!}\n=\\frac{6!}{3!}\n=\\frac{6\\cdot5\\cdot4\\cdot3!}{3!}\n=6\\cdot5\\cdot4=120.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(120\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
